  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a compound that interacts with a common downstream target, 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which show a direct or indirect link between Mollicellin N and the enzyme of interest. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N may inhibit the activity of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which then affects the enzyme responsible for histone modification. The presence of a consistent target pathway across different paths strengthens the hypothesis that Mollicellin N exerts its effect through this specific molecular mechanism. The integration of multiple evidence streams supports a mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
